WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.320
I think I need to lose a little weight.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.080
President Trump just announced tariffs on fifty billion dollars of Chinese goods,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.800
and half the planet seems to be screaming about a trade war. Neither the administration nor its critics are right

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.240
nor its critics are right because the tariffs will actually have little impact. The administration is

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.090
right that China coerces US companies
into transferring technology, and steals

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.720
other intellectual property outright.
They're also right that the WTO has

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.820
failed to prevent this and US action is
overdue. But the 25 percent tariff on 50

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.630
billion dollars will only cut imports
from China by about $20 billion. Imports

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.489
from China rose twice that much in 2017.
We won't even notice these tariffs. For

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:42.270
that reason, China doesn't have much
reason to act on its own to retaliate.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.750
They will certainly threaten to do so, in
part to scare other countries from

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.500
copying the US. But they need trade with
the US more than the US needs trade with

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.550
China. So it's in China's interest for
this dispute to stay limited. Right now,

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.420
this is a tempest in a teapot, but
eventually people are going to notice

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.559
that very little has actually changed,
and that "eventually" may coincide with

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.240
the start of the 2020 presidential
election campaign. We're not done with this yet.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.200
What do you think about taking a
tougher stand on China? Let us know in

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.500
your comments. Also, let us know what
other topics you'd like our scholars to

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.950
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like
and subscribe for more research and

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.970
videos from AEI.

